Here
\begin{align*}
   \mqty(a_0 & b_0 \\mathfrak c_0 & d_0 )  =  \frac{1}{k} \mqty(k & -f_2 r_1r_2 \\ & 1) \mqty(a_1 & b_1 \\ c_1 & d_1)  = \frac{1}{k} \mqty(k a_1-f_2 r_1r_2  c_1 & k b_1-f_2 r_1r_2  d_1 \\ c_1 & d_1) = \frac{1}{k} \mqty(a_2 & b_2 \\ c_2 &  d_2).
\end{align*}
Thus, summing over $f_2$ and combining the variables (using $(k,r_1r_2)=1$) we get
\begin{align*}
